   "msg": "Scripted browser HTTP response",
   "http": "response",
   "response_content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>OIDF Conformance: Processing Implicit Callback</title>\n\n    <!-- Served to the suite's own headless browser: only suite-hosted assets and no components; the chrome\n         below reuses the cts-navbar / cts-page-head / cts-footer rules from oidf-app.css -->\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/css/oidf-tokens.css\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/css/layout.css\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/css/oidf-app.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n    <nav class=\"cts-nav\">\n        <a class=\"cts-brand\" href=\"/plans.html\">\n            <img src=\"/images/openid-dark.svg\" alt=\"OpenID Foundation\" width=\"93\" height=\"28\">\n            <span class=\"cts-brand-name\">CONFORMANCE SUITE</span>\n        </a>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main class=\"narrow-page\">\n        <div id=\"waiting\">\n            <div class=\"oidf-page-head\">\n                <div class=\"oidf-page-head-text\">\n                    <h1 class=\"t-title oidf-page-head-title\">Please wait...</h1>\n                    <p class=\"t-meta oidf-page-head-sub\">Processing response from authorization server</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <p>The server should have returned its results as part of a URI fragment. This data normally stays in the browser and needs to be explicitly sent to the test framework for further processing.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"complete\" hidden>\n            <div class=\"oidf-page-head\">\n                <div class=\"oidf-page-head-text\">\n                    <h1 class=\"t-title oidf-page-head-title\">Response received</h1>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <p>The response has been sent to the server for processing. You may return to <a href=\"/log-detail.html?log=nxj1WKFUGIfh6dO\">the test results page.</a></p>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"rejected\" hidden>\n            <div class=\"oidf-page-head\">\n                <div class=\"oidf-page-head-text\">\n                    <h1 class=\"t-title oidf-page-head-title\">Response not accepted</h1>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n            <p>The test framework did not accept the response: HTTP <span id=\"rejected-reason\"></span></p>\n            <p>The test may no longer be waiting for this callback. Check the test log on <a href=\"/log-detail.html?log=nxj1WKFUGIfh6dO\">the test results page.</a></p>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"oidf-footer pageFooter t-meta\">OpenID Foundation conformance suite</footer>\n\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\n        var submitComplete = false;\n        function assumeComplete() {\n            if (submitComplete) {\n                return;\n            }\n            console.log(\"assumeComplete workaround for https://gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite/-/issues/766 activated - assuming post has completed as 5 seconds have elapsed\")\n            // add a hidden tag so that Selenium can detect we're done processing\n\n            document.getElementById('complete').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', '<span id=\"submission_complete\" hidden></span>');\n        }\n\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n\n            var hash = window.location.hash;\n\n            // workaround https://gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite/-/issues/766 by assuming that the post completes\n            // after 5 seconds\n            var timeoutId = setTimeout(function(){ assumeComplete(); }, 5000);\n\n            function createxhr() {\n                var xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();\n                xhr.open('POST', \"https:\\/\\/localhost.emobix.co.uk:8443\\/test\\/a\\/clavaris-basic\\/implicit\\/aQp7BFT2oumamOlju1jH\", true);\n                xhr.setRequestHeader('Content-type', 'text/plain');\n                xhr.onload = function () {\n                    submitComplete = true;\n                    var accepted = xhr.status >= 200 && xhr.status < 300;\n                    var outcome = document.getElementById(accepted ? 'complete' : 'rejected');\n                    if (!accepted) {\n                        var reason = xhr.status + \" \" + xhr.responseText;\n                        console.log(\"implicit submit rejected: \" + reason);\n                        document.getElementById('rejected-reason').textContent = reason;\n                    }\n                    document.getElementById('waiting').hidden = true;\n                    outcome.hidden = false;\n                    // add a hidden tag so that Selenium can detect we're done processing\n                    document.getElementById('complete').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', '<span id=\"submission_complete\" hidden></span>');\n                };\n                xhr.onabort = function () {\n                    console.log(\"implicit submit abort\")\n                };\n                xhr.ontimeout = function () {\n                    console.log(\"implicit submit timeout\")\n                };\n                return xhr;\n            }\n\n            var xhr = createxhr();\n            xhr.onerror = function () {\n                console.log(\"implicit submit error (trying again in 2 seconds): \" + xhr.status + \" \" + xhr.responseText);\n                // workaround for https://gitlab.com/openid/conformance-suite/-/issues/1458\n                clearTimeout(timeoutId);\n                timeoutId = setTimeout(function(){ assumeComplete(); }, 5000);\n                setTimeout(function() {\n                    var retry = createxhr();\n                    retry.onerror = function () {\n                        console.log(\"second implicit submit error: \" + retry.status + \" \" + retry.responseText);\n                    };\n                    retry.send(hash);\n                }, 2000);\n            };\n            xhr.send(hash);\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
